---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Branding & Style Guide" metaTitle="Brand Guidelines: Name, Logo and Colours" description="Lightning Piggy brand guidelines: how to write the name, when LightningPiggy is allowed, logos for light and dark backgrounds, and our pink and yellow colours.">
  <section class="py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <header class="text-center mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Branding & Style Guide</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          How to write the name, plus the official logos and colours for Lightning Piggy.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Naming -->
      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Naming</h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
          <!-- The name -->
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-6">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-yellow-light text-gray-700 text-xs font-semibold rounded-full">The name</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Lightning Piggy</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">Two words, with a space. Use it everywhere people read the name.</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Use for:</p>
            <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-1.5">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Website, marketing and social posts
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                News, blog posts and articles
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Guides, documentation and release notes
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Product names, packaging and talks
              </li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl">
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Examples</p>
              <div class="space-y-1 text-sm text-gray-700">
                <p class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">"Lightning Piggy helps smart savers stack sats."</p>
                <p class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">"Meet Lightning Piggy, the Bitcoin piggy bank."</p>
                <p class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">"Lightning Piggy firmware v2.1 is out."</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- Where a space is not allowed -->
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-6">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
              <span class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-pink-light/50 text-pink text-xs font-semibold rounded-full">No space</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">LightningPiggy</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">No space, only where a space is not allowed.</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-2">Use for:</p>
            <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-1.5">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Repository and package names
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Code (classes, functions, variables, filenames)
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Usernames, handles, and hashtags
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Web addresses and file names (in lower case: lightningpiggy)
              </li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl">
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Examples</p>
              <div class="space-y-1 text-sm">
                <code class="block text-gray-700 bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">class LightningPiggy</code>
                <code class="block text-gray-700 bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">#LightningPiggy</code>
                <code class="block text-gray-700 bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">lightningpiggy-logo.svg</code>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <!-- Capitalisation & Consistency -->
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Capitalisation</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-3">Always capitalise both words:</p>
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-green-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
                <span class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">Lightning Piggy</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-green-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>
                <span class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">LightningPiggy <span class="font-normal text-gray-500">(code, handles and hashtags only)</span></span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-400 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12" /></svg>
                <code class="text-sm text-gray-500">lightningpiggy</code>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-400 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12" /></svg>
                <code class="text-sm text-gray-500">Lightningpiggy</code>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-400 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12" /></svg>
                <code class="text-sm text-gray-500">LIGHTNING PIGGY</code>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Consistency</h3>
            <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 space-y-3">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                In any sentence, heading or title, write <strong>Lightning Piggy</strong>.
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Keep <strong>LightningPiggy</strong> for code, handles and hashtags, where a space can't go.
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                Avoid common typos such as <code class="text-red-400 bg-red-50 px-1 rounded">Lighting Piggy</code>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                <span class="text-pink mt-0.5">&#8226;</span>
                When unsure, write <strong>Lightning Piggy</strong>.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Logo -->
      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Logo</h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-8 flex flex-col items-center">
            <img
              src="/images/branding/lightningpiggy-logo.svg"
              alt="Lightning Piggy logo in pink and yellow"
              class="h-16 w-auto mb-4"
            />
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-700">Pink & Yellow</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">For light backgrounds</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl border border-gray-700 p-8 flex flex-col items-center">
            <img
              src="/images/branding/lightningpiggy-logo-white-yellow.svg"
              alt="Lightning Piggy logo in white and yellow"
              class="h-16 w-auto mb-4"
            />
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-300">White & Yellow</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">For dark backgrounds</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Colours -->
      <div class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Colours</h2>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
            <div class="h-24" style="background-color: #EC008C;"></div>
            <div class="p-4">
              <p class="font-bold text-gray-900">Accent Pink</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Outline & primary accent</p>
              <code class="block mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 bg-gray-50 px-2 py-1 rounded">#EC008C</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
            <div class="h-24" style="background-color: #F0BCD7;"></div>
            <div class="p-4">
              <p class="font-bold text-gray-900">Light Pink</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Fill & background</p>
              <code class="block mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 bg-gray-50 px-2 py-1 rounded">#F0BCD7</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden">
            <div class="h-24" style="background-color: #FFDB00;"></div>
            <div class="p-4">
              <p class="font-bold text-gray-900">Lightning Yellow</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-0.5">Lightning bolt accent</p>
              <code class="block mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 bg-gray-50 px-2 py-1 rounded">#FFDB00</code>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Rationale -->
      <div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl text-center">
        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
          <strong>Lightning Piggy</strong> is the name: two words read naturally for everyone.
          <strong>LightningPiggy</strong> stays where a space isn't possible, such as code, handles and hashtags.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-3">
          Proposed changes to this guide should be discussed via a <a href="https://github.com/LightningPiggy" class="text-pink hover:underline">pull request</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
